# Migration-owner scratch stacks (docs/DEVELOPMENT-PLAN.md wave 2,
# supabase/config.toml's reserved stack blocks) — a workdir copy of
# config.toml with real local ports, never tracked. Globbed rather than
# listed one suffix at a time: each new migration-owner lane reserves
# the next free "+100 ports" block (bcion-lite-migration-3 was the
# first one to actually need it) and this pattern should never need
# editing again just because a new one opened.
.supabase-migration/
.supabase-migration-*/

# Node (if Playwright/e2e tooling adds a package.json later)
node_modules/

# Migration owner's own second local Supabase stack (supabase/config.toml
# "SECOND STACK FOR THE MIGRATION LANE"; CONSENT-4 is the first to open
# it) — scratch, per-worktree, never shared/tracked.
.supabase-migration/

